# {{PROJECT_NAME}} - Epilogue
# The convergence point — every story branch routes here via [goto].
# This file is the last arc in the chain: prologue → branch(es) → epilogue.
# In a real game, this would contain your ending scene, credits sequence,
# post-game unlock screen, or a route-specific epilogue based on variables.

@scenario {{SCENARIO_PREFIX}}_epilogue
@include {{CHARACTERS_INCLUDE}}

{{BG_DECL}}@label start
{{BG_START}}[show lavender center {{LAVENDER_EXPR}}]
[wait 200]

# ─── Epilogue Scene ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# The player arrives here after completing a branch.
# You can use [if] blocks to show different endings based on variables
# set during the story — e.g. [if courage >= 3] for a brave ending.

Lavender: You've reached the {b}epilogue{/b} — the final arc in the story chain.
[show lavender center talking]
Lavender: You got here because the branch demo file ended with:
narrator: {color=#8888cc}[goto {{SCENARIO_PREFIX}}_epilogue:start]{/color}
narrator: That's the same cross-file navigation pattern the prologue used to reach the branch.

Lavender: In a real project, this is where you'd put your ending. What goes here depends on your game:
narrator: {b}Linear story{/b} — a single ending scene, credits, and [end].
narrator: {b}Branching story{/b} — use [if] to check route variables and show different endings.
narrator: {b}Post-game{/b} — unlock a gallery, new game+, or bonus content before [end].

[show lavender left talking]
Lavender: Here's what a branching ending would look like in script:
narrator: {color=#8888cc}[if route == "brave"]{/color}
narrator: {color=#8888cc}Lavender: You stood your ground when it mattered.{/color}
narrator: {color=#8888cc}[elif route == "cautious"]{/color}
narrator: {color=#8888cc}Lavender: You chose carefully. That takes its own kind of strength.{/color}
narrator: {color=#8888cc}[else]{/color}
narrator: {color=#8888cc}Lavender: Every path leads somewhere worth arriving.{/color}
narrator: {color=#8888cc}[endif]{/color}

[show lavender center happy]
Lavender: The full arc structure of this project:
narrator: {color=#8888cc}prologue{/color} → {color=#8888cc}branch demo{/color} → {color=#8888cc}epilogue (you are here){/color}
narrator: Open the Story Map at {b}{{STORY_MAP_PATH}}{/b} in the editor to see the arc graph visually.

Lavender: That's the complete demo. To start building your own game:
narrator: {b}1.{/b} Replace the prologue content with your opening scene.
narrator: {b}2.{/b} Replace the branch demo with your first chapter or route.
narrator: {b}3.{/b} Replace this epilogue with your ending.
narrator: {b}4.{/b} Add more branch files as your story grows — one per chapter or route.

# ─── End ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# [end] terminates the game session. The engine returns to the main menu.
# In a real game, you might show credits before calling [end],
# or [goto] to a post-game scene before ending.

[end]
